%% Data flow: hold a space when the response is lost (processing succeeded, delivery failed)
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor D as Driver
    participant App as Mobile app
    participant BS as Base station / wireless
    participant S as Web service
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    D->>App: Tap "Hold space A-01, 10:00-12:00"
    App->>App: operationId = UUIDv4, save to pending store
    App->>BS: POST /reservations (Idempotency-Key: operationId)
    BS->>S: request
    S->>DB: BEGIN, insert operation + reservation(HELD), COMMIT
    DB-->>S: committed
    S--xBS: 201 Created (response LOST - link dropped)
    App->>App: timeout after 10 s, show "Checking your reservation..."
    Note over App: Do NOT create a new operationId
    App->>BS: (reconnected) GET /operations/{operationId}
    BS->>S: request
    S->>DB: SELECT operation
    DB-->>S: SUCCEEDED, stored 201 body
    S-->>App: 200 {outcome: SUCCEEDED, response: reservation HELD}
    App->>App: remove from pending store, update cache
    App-->>D: "Space A-01 is held until 10:12 - pay to confirm"
    alt operation not found (404)
        App->>S: POST /reservations again with SAME operationId
        S-->>App: 201 (first execution) or stored response (replay)
    end
